            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>
          Two-seat cars, including the Huracán and the {label(bySlug('sf90'))}, belong to a different evening: a drive, two people, and a sober driver. They are a poor fit for Bayfront Park, a Beach concert, or a night that ends after midnight in traffic. Those pages are linked above.
        </p>

        <figure class="not-prose my-10">
          <img src={porschePhoto.src} srcset={porschePhoto.srcSet} sizes="(min-width: 1140px) 760px, 100vw" width={porschePhoto.width} height={porschePhoto.height} alt={porschePhoto.alt} loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="w-full h-auto rounded-2xl" />
          <figcaption class="text-black/60 text-sm mt-3">The {label(porsche)} fits when the drive is the plan. It is the wrong car for a group leaving after midnight.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h2 id="chauffeur-or-drive-yourself">Chauffeur or drive yourself</h2>

        <p>
          If anyone in the car will be drinking, do not drive. A rented exotic is not an exception. The straightforward plan is a chauffeur, or a designated driver who is actually staying sober.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/chauffeur-service-miami">Chauffeur service</a> is from {usd(chauffeurHourly.amount)} an hour in the {label(gls)}, including the driver and fuel. Send the itinerary and we will confirm an all-in rate before you book.
        </p>

        <figure class="not-prose my-10">
          <img src={seatsPhoto.src} srcset={seatsPhoto.srcSet} sizes="(min-width: 1140px) 760px, 100vw" width={seatsPhoto.width} height={seatsPhoto.height} alt={seatsPhoto.alt} loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="w-full h-auto rounded-2xl" />
          <figcaption class="text-black/60 text-sm mt-3">{gls.seats} executive seats, with room for jackets. That is why this is the default for the night.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p>
          A self-driven car still makes sense when the night is one venue, someone is not drinking, and you want the car the next morning. On New Year's Eve, build in time and do not count on leaving a car next to the fireworks.
        </p>
        <p>
          Day-rate math and what a Maybach day includes are in the guide linked above, How much to rent a Maybach in Miami.
        </p>

        <h2 id="how-to-book">How to book</h2>

        <p>
          Send the dates, the car, and the pickup point in the form at the top of this page. The fleet and the pricing page are linked above. You need to be {minimumAge} or older, with a valid driver's license and qualifying insurance. The refundable deposit is {deposit.display}. The {label(sto)} is the exception: drivers {sto.minimumAge} and over, and a {sto.deposit.display} deposit. Rentals include {perDay} miles a day{mileage.pooled ? ', pooled across the booking' : ''}. Delivery is {miami.display} each way in Miami, including Miami International, Brickell and South Beach. Downtown Miami and Edgewater are {downtown.display} each way. Fort Lauderdale is {fll.display} each way. At the end, return the car to our location, or we pick it up for a fee agreed in your quote. Hours are {hoursSummary}.
        </p>

